<title>GERMANY: Telekom -to pay off debts with issue income.</title>
<headline>Telekom -to pay off debts with issue income.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1996-11-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>German telecommunications company Deutsche Telekom AG said on Sunday that it would use the 20 billion marks or so raised in its first-ever share placement to pay off outstanding debt.</p>
<p>The company's chief financial officer Joachim Kroeske told a news conference that the proceeds would be used &quot;completely&quot; to settle debts. Telekom said earlier today it would issue 713 million shares at a price of 28.50 marks each.</p>
<p>--William Boston, Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
